  "upload": {
    "title": "How Does Tesla Build a Car Every 10 Seconds? 🚗 #shorts",
    "description": "Tesla's Cybercab line is designed to roll out a car every 10 seconds. How? 🚗\n\nInstead of building a car like a box, one station after another, Tesla's \"unboxed\" process splits the Cybercab into modules (front, rear, floor and interior) that are built in parallel and joined in one final step. The body panels are molded in color, so there's no paint shop. Tesla says the line targets a cycle time under 10 seconds, versus about 34 seconds for a Model Y, with 5 seconds as the long-term goal.\n\nBuilt faster than you can find a parking spot. 👇\n\nSubscribe to Top Techs for more mind-blowing tech in under a minute.",
